{"kind":"doc","route":"/guide/components/composition-boundaries","title":"Composition boundaries: sealComponent","blocks":[{"t":"heading","level":1,"id":"composition-boundaries-sealcomponent","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Composition boundaries: "},{"t":"code","text":"sealComponent"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"A component's type remembers two different things:"}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":""},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"its contracts"}]},{"t":"text","text":" — props and inputs, the services it still needs"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"("},{"t":"code","text":"ComponentDepsOf"},{"t":"text","text":"), the exceptions a parent must catch, a "},{"t":"code","text":"heading()"},{"t":"text","text":" a"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"parent must wrap in "},{"t":"code","text":"headingSection"},{"t":"text","text":", style channels, content requirements;"}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":""},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"the shape of the tree its template renders"}]},{"t":"text","text":" — every element, and the"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"full type of every child component, recursively."}]}]]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"A parent checks the contracts. Only typed locators and template contracts read"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"the shape. Each component computes its contracts once. The shape, however,"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"grows with the depth of the tree, and some composition sites re-expand it:"}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"a node choosing between two components ("},{"t":"code","text":"flag ? A() : B()"},{"t":"text","text":");"}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"a component passed to a slot, mounted as a "},{"t":"code","text":"forNode"},{"t":"text","text":" row, or compared"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"against a generic constraint;"}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"the declaration ("},{"t":"code","text":".d.ts"},{"t":"text","text":") of an exported component, which may fail with"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"code","text":"TS7056: The inferred type of this node exceeds the maximum length the compiler will serialize"},{"t":"text","text":"."}]}]]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"code","text":"sealComponent"},{"t":"text","text":" keeps the contracts and drops the shape."}]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"usage","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Usage"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Keep the definition plain, and seal the component where it is composed:"}]},{"t":"code","lines":[{"tokens":[{"text":"// workspace-browser.ts","kind":"comment"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"import","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" { craftComponent } ","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"from","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"'@craft-ts/component'","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":";","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[]},{"tokens":[{"text":"export","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"const","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"WorkspaceBrowser"},{"text":" "},{"text":"=","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"craftComponent","kind":"function"},{"text":"(","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"  "},{"text":"'WorkspaceBrowser'","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":",","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"  { providers: [","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"provideWorkspace","kind":"function"},{"text":"()] },","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"  "},{"text":"function*","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" () {","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"    "},{"text":"const","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"workspace"},{"text":" "},{"text":"=","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"yield*","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"Workspace","kind":"function"},{"text":"();","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"    "},{"text":"return","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"div","kind":"function"},{"text":"([","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"Toolbar","kind":"function"},{"text":"(), ","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"FileTree","kind":"function"},{"text":"(), ","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"Preview","kind":"function"},{"text":"()]);","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"  },","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":");","kind":"punctuation"}]}],"filename":"","language":"ts","numbered":false,"firstLine":1},{"t":"code","lines":[{"tokens":[{"text":"// shell.ts","kind":"comment"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"import","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" { craftComponent, div, sealComponent } ","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"from","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"'@craft-ts/component'","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":";","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"import","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" { WorkspaceBrowser } ","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"from","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"'./workspace-browser'","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":";","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[]},{"tokens":[{"text":"const","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"SealedWorkspaceBrowser"},{"text":" "},{"text":"=","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"sealComponent","kind":"function"},{"text":"(WorkspaceBrowser);","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[]},{"tokens":[{"text":"export","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"const","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"Shell"},{"text":" "},{"text":"=","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"craftComponent","kind":"function"},{"text":"(","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"'Shell'","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":", {}, () ","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"=>","kind":"keyword"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"  "},{"text":"div","kind":"function"},{"text":"([flag ","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"?","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"SealedWorkspaceBrowser","kind":"function"},{"text":"() ","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":":","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"Welcome","kind":"function"},{"text":"()]),","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":");","kind":"punctuation"}]}],"filename":"","language":"ts","numbered":false,"firstLine":1},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"The component itself is returned untouched. Sealing only changes what its type"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"remembers, so there is nothing to change at runtime. Keeping the definition"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"unsealed keeps its own tests able to reach into its template (see"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"link","href":"#testing-a-sealed-component","external":false,"children":[{"t":"text","text":"Testing a sealed component"}]},{"t":"text","text":")."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"A library that publishes declaration files seals in its public index instead,"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"so the "},{"t":"code","text":".d.ts"},{"t":"text","text":" no longer has to spell the template out (TS7056):"}]},{"t":"code","lines":[{"tokens":[{"text":"// index.ts of the library","kind":"comment"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"import","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" { WorkspaceBrowser ","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"as","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" WorkspaceBrowserComponent } ","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"from","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"'./workspace-browser'","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":";","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"import","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" { sealComponent } ","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"from","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"'@craft-ts/component'","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":";","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[]},{"tokens":[{"text":"export","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"const","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"WorkspaceBrowser"},{"text":" "},{"text":"=","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"sealComponent","kind":"function"},{"text":"(WorkspaceBrowserComponent);","kind":"punctuation"}]}],"filename":"","language":"ts","numbered":false,"firstLine":1},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"what-a-sealed-component-keeps","children":[{"t":"text","text":"What a sealed component keeps"}]},{"t":"table","head":[[{"t":"text","text":"Contract"}],[{"t":"text","text":"Still checked on a sealed component"}]],"rows":[[[{"t":"text","text":"Props and required inputs"}],[{"t":"text","text":"yes: a missing input is still a compile error"}]],[[{"t":"text","text":"Dependency contract ("},{"t":"code","text":"ComponentDepsOf"},{"t":"text","text":", "},{"t":"code","text":"RouteCheckedDI"},{"t":"text","text":")"}],[{"t":"text","text":"yes: the component and every parent rendering it"}]],[[{"t":"text","text":"Initialization exceptions"}],[{"t":"text","text":"yes: rendering it without "},{"t":"code","text":"catchNode"},{"t":"text","text":" is still refused"}]],[[{"t":"text","text":"Field exceptions"}],[{"t":"text","text":"yes"}]],[[{"t":"code","text":"heading()"},{"t":"text","text":" need"}],[{"t":"text","text":"yes: the parent must still wrap it in "},{"t":"code","text":"headingSection"}]],[[{"t":"text","text":"Style channels and content requirements"}],[{"t":"text","text":"yes"}]],[[{"t":"code","text":".pipe(...)"}],[{"t":"text","text":"yes, with the same operators and checks"}]],[[{"t":"text","text":"Typed locators / template contracts reaching "},{"t":"em","children":[{"t":"text","text":"into"}]},{"t":"text","text":" it"}],[{"t":"text","text":"no, they stop at the sealed boundary"}]]]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"when-to-seal","children":[{"t":"text","text":"When to seal"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Sealing is one remedy for a type that grew too deep, not a default. Reach for"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"it when TypeScript reports one of these on a component tree:"}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"code","text":"TS2589: Type instantiation is excessively deep and possibly infinite"},{"t":"text","text":";"}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"code","text":"TS2321: Excessive stack depth comparing types"},{"t":"text","text":";"}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"code","text":"TS7056: The inferred type of this node exceeds the maximum length the compiler will serialize"},{"t":"text","text":";"}]}]]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"or when "},{"t":"code","text":"tsc --extendedDiagnostics"},{"t":"text","text":" shows composition dominating the"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"instantiation count. Seal at the boundary the error points to: a node"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"choosing between components, a slot, a "},{"t":"code","text":"forNode"},{"t":"text","text":" row, an exported component."},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"Other remedies remain: split one huge template into child components, and for"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"a route collection, split it with "},{"t":"code","text":"loadChildren"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"("},{"t":"link","href":"/craft/guide/routing/scaling","external":false,"children":[{"t":"text","text":"Scaling routes"}]},{"t":"text","text":")."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"A sealed component costs about the same per nesting level as a plain one. The"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"difference shows where the plain one re-expands its tree: a node choosing"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"between two plain components overflows (TS2321) around 14 levels, while sealed"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"components compile 32 levels down. "},{"t":"code","text":"npm run type-budget"},{"t":"text","text":" checks these figures"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"on every change."}]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"testing-a-sealed-component","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Testing a sealed component"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"The register of "},{"t":"code","text":"setupCraftComponentTemplateTest"},{"t":"text","text":" — the services a test must"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"mock or declare — is the same whether a component, or a child it renders, is"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"sealed. Locating by tag, role, label or attribute works the same too."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"What stops at a sealed boundary is everything that reads the template's"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"types: content locators ("},{"t":"code","text":"result.locator('span', { content: 'status' })"},{"t":"text","text":") and"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"template contracts ("},{"t":"code","text":"TemplateRendersNamedElementWhen"},{"t":"text","text":"). Test the unsealed"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"component, which is why the definition stays plain and the seal sits where the"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"component is used:"}]},{"t":"code","lines":[{"tokens":[{"text":"// workspace-browser.spec.ts — the plain component keeps typed locators.","kind":"comment"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"const","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"result"},{"text":" "},{"text":"=","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"await","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"setupCraftComponentTemplateTest","kind":"function"},{"text":"(WorkspaceBrowser, {","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"  inputs: {},","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"  register: { workspace: ","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"'provided'","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":" },","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"});","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"result.","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"locator","kind":"function"},{"text":"(","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"'span'","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":", { content: ","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"'workspaceName'","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":" });","kind":"punctuation"}]}],"filename":"","language":"ts","numbered":false,"firstLine":1},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"A parent test cannot locate by content inside a sealed child. That is usually"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"right: a parent test should not depend on how a child renders."}]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"never-type-a-component-by-hand","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Never type a component by hand"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Before: the annotation suggested to hide a component's template drops its"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"contracts with it."}]},{"t":"code","lines":[{"tokens":[{"text":"// ✗ drops the dependency contract, the exceptions and the heading need","kind":"comment"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"export","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"const","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"Panel"},{"text":":","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"CraftComponent","kind":"type"},{"text":"<","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"PropsFromFactory","kind":"type"},{"text":"<() ","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"=>","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"never","kind":"type"},{"text":">> ","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"=","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" PanelImpl;","kind":"punctuation"}]}],"filename":"","language":"ts","numbered":false,"firstLine":1},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"After:"}]},{"t":"code","lines":[{"tokens":[{"text":"// ✓ keeps every contract, drops only the template tree","kind":"comment"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"export","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"const","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"Panel"},{"text":" "},{"text":"=","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"sealComponent","kind":"function"},{"text":"(PanelImpl);","kind":"punctuation"}]}],"filename":"","language":"ts","numbered":false,"firstLine":1},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Why it matters: "},{"t":"code","text":"CraftComponent<Props>"},{"t":"text","text":" has no dependency contract. A DI proof"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"on that component, or on any component rendering it, used to answer "},{"t":"code","text":"true"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"even with a provider missing. It now fails with:"}]},{"t":"code","lines":[{"tokens":[{"text":"The dependency contract of a component rendered in this component is unknown:"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"the value is not a component, or a component was typed by hand. Pass the"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"component itself to ComponentDepsOf, and seal a component with"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"sealComponent(Component) instead of typing it"}]}],"filename":"","language":"","numbered":false,"firstLine":1},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"code","text":"craft-ts/no-craft-component-return-type"},{"t":"text","text":" reports the annotation in the"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"editor. It offers to remove it as a suggestion, not as an automatic fix,"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"because removing it can change what compiles. Use "},{"t":"code","text":"sealComponent(...)"},{"t":"text","text":" when"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"the annotation was there to keep the type small."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"When a declaration needs to name the type, use "},{"t":"code","text":"SealedComponent<typeof PanelImpl>"},{"t":"text","text":"."},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"Never write the "},{"t":"code","text":"CraftComponent<…>"},{"t":"text","text":" arguments yourself."}]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"see-also","children":[{"t":"text","text":"See Also"}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"link","href":"/craft/guide/components/","external":false,"children":[{"t":"text","text":"Components"}]}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"link","href":"/craft/guide/routing/scaling","external":false,"children":[{"t":"text","text":"Scaling routes"}]},{"t":"text","text":": DI proofs and when they fail closed"}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"link","href":"/craft/guide/testing/components","external":false,"children":[{"t":"text","text":"Testing components"}]}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"link","href":"/craft/guide/routing/eslint-rules","external":false,"children":[{"t":"text","text":"ESLint rules"}]}]}]]}],"outline":[{"level":2,"id":"usage","text":"Usage"},{"level":2,"id":"what-a-sealed-component-keeps","text":"What a sealed component keeps"},{"level":2,"id":"when-to-seal","text":"When to seal"},{"level":2,"id":"testing-a-sealed-component","text":"Testing a sealed component"},{"level":2,"id":"never-type-a-component-by-hand","text":"Never type a component by hand"},{"level":2,"id":"see-also","text":"See Also"}]}